From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: the shell binds touchpad gestures of three fingers
 or more

A swipe, pinch or hold of three fingers or more goes to the shell when
it grabs one (DomicileHost.grabGesture), instead of to the window under
the pointer. Two fingers stay the page's.

- `libinput_event_converter`: HandleShellGesture offers each libinput
  gesture to the NativeGestureSink before the pinch path. A swipe or
  hold the shell does not take is dropped, as before; an untaken pinch
  goes on to the page. Disabling the device cancels a taken gesture.
- `wayland_zwp_pointer_gestures`: when nested, binds the host's swipe
  gesture too, and offers swipes, pinches and holds to the sink first.
- `ui/events` builds the sink; `ui/events/types` exports NativeGesture.
- bindings: build DomicileGestureEvent and its init dictionary.
- The test server answers get_swipe_gesture.

The sink, the event and the grab are new files under src/.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
